    <h2 class="p6-section-title">Multi-layer analog + electronic redundancy</h2>
    <p class="p6-section-lead">
        Phase 6 prioritizes reliability through redundant safety systems. Unlike modern vehicles
        that depend on single-point-of-failure electronic controls, this steam car uses analog
        mechanical backup systems for all critical functions. The boiler (most dangerous component)
        is over-engineered with hard pressure relief, thermal shutdown, and a secondary emergency
        pressure bleed system powered by Battery B. Crash zones are reinforced. Weight is kept below
        2000 lbs to maintain passenger safety and agility.
    </p>

